{"journal_version":1,"sequence":11,"replace_from":17,"message_count":18,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Verification passed.\n\n## Change\n\n`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`\n- Replaced the one-shot `setTimeout` in the mount effect with a `schedule(onDone)` helper that clears any pending timer before arming a new 120 ms timer, plus `clearScheduled()` for unmount cleanup (single `timerRef`, so no overlapping timers are possible).\n- Added `retry()`: sets state to `loading` synchronously (panel immediately shows `Checking service…`), then schedules the same 120 ms delay resolving to `success` (`All changes are synced.`), regardless of `?sync=error` still being in the URL. It's a `type=\"button\"` with local state only — no navigation/reload, and no parent/task-selection state is touched.\n- Added the `Retry sync` button inside the existing `role=\"alert\"` error block; it only exists in the error branch, so the success path at `/` never renders it and it disappears after success.\n\n`src/styles.css`\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 6px; }` so the button aligns within the existing error grid; existing global button styling, focus-visible outline, and error/success colors are untouched.\n\n## Commands actually run\n\n`verify_frontend` → `npm run verify:agent` (`npm run build && npm run test:public`): exit 0 — tsc + vite build succeeded, 6/6 public Playwright tests passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- The retry result is hard-coded to success (per the acceptance criteria), so retrying while `/` is actually served `?sync=error` will report success; if the intent is to re-probe the URL, that's a follow-up.\n- No new automated test covers the retry flow (existing public tests were left untouched by design); it was verified only via build + existing suite, not by a dedicated browser assertion.","response_items":[{"id":"0ab408b0-b5f8-4c5b-bc84-3137b38af2a4","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Verification passed.\n\n## Change\n\n`src/components/AsyncPanel.tsx`\n- Replaced the one-shot `setTimeout` in the mount effect with a `schedule(onDone)` helper that clears any pending timer before arming a new 120 ms timer, plus `clearScheduled()` for unmount cleanup (single `timerRef`, so no overlapping timers are possible).\n- Added `retry()`: sets state to `loading` synchronously (panel immediately shows `Checking service…`), then schedules the same 120 ms delay resolving to `success` (`All changes are synced.`), regardless of `?sync=error` still being in the URL. It's a `type=\"button\"` with local state only — no navigation/reload, and no parent/task-selection state is touched.\n- Added the `Retry sync` button inside the existing `role=\"alert\"` error block; it only exists in the error branch, so the success path at `/` never renders it and it disappears after success.\n\n`src/styles.css`\n- Added `.sync-retry { justify-self: start; margin-top: 6px; }` so the button aligns within the existing error grid; existing global button styling, focus-visible outline, and error/success colors are untouched.\n\n## Commands actually run\n\n`verify_frontend` → `npm run verify:agent` (`npm run build && npm run test:public`): exit 0 — tsc + vite build succeeded, 6/6 public Playwright tests passed.\n\n## Remaining risks\n\n- The retry result is hard-coded to success (per the acceptance criteria), so retrying while `/` is actually served `?sync=error` will report success; if the intent is to re-probe the URL, that's a follow-up.\n- No new automated test covers the retry flow (existing public tests were left untouched by design); it was verified only via build + existing suite, not by a dedicated browser assertion.","type":"output_text","logprobs":[]}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":"final_answer"}],"timestamp":"2026-11-22T15:51:11.149833+00:00"}],"meta":{"snapshot_version":1,"aid":0,"role":"workflow_agent","model":"deepseek-flash","session_state":{"used_tokens":37243,"context_tokens":7156,"ste